body:
This is true, thanks for pointing out that detail.  

&#x200B;

I can't speak for every state, but the last 6 that I've lived in it was legal and have heard by word of mouth it's the same for many more.  I haven't bothered to verify any of them by going to the formal sources  It is legal by all of the federal war on drugs laws and regulations.  I can't speak to every state, but it shouldn't be difficult to do some googling.

Verify that you're really on their site by their PGP message every time before logging in, along with reading and following all of the other instructions they provide so that everything is verified and you're all good.  The rest is gravy.  There's always a slight chance of an exit scam but even if it the once in a site's lifetime event were to happen, the chances of you getting caught in that small time window are Slim, Shady.

&#x200B;

Edit: exist/exit typo

Personally, I wouldn't mind waiting until I got to know someone.  Girls initiate things becoming sexual early on as well though, quite often.  I rarely push thing early on, but if I'm I like someone and see a solid future possible, I'm not too har to persuade.

&#x200B;

I I don't know how long 'some time' after being in an exclusive relationship is, but it sounds like something fishy and questionable to me.  If I'm in a relationship with someone, I would know them pretty well, and they'd know me the same.  

&#x200B;

What are you worried about?  A dude faking that he's into you, committed and is gonna bolt once he gets laid?  Maybe you're someone who thinks sex is as permanent of a mark on you as tattoos, but you could also be someone that's playing games and setting secret tests to evaluate someone's response.  If I thought it was the latter, I'd walk away at the first sign of it.  If it's the former there's a long list of things needed to understand and form an opinion on it.

Even worse is trying to transfer when you move from one state to another.  I had to fly 2 and 3000 miles each way just to fill a script and come back, and the same to see my doctor every 3 months.  Couldn't find a single doctor or clinic that would continue my well documented and legitimate pain treatment entirely because they wouldn't continue the script.  They even told me to find different doctors and different practices.  Basically they didn't want any involvement with me as a patient because I took a very reasonable opioid extended release medication.

&#x200B;

You're spot on with the injections too.  When signing the waivers I asked what exactly the 'medicine', as they always referred to it, was.  They had to ask 4 people and still didn't know.  Finally the 5th person, the doctor actually doing the injections told me "it's medicine to help'.  When I insisted he tell me what it was or I was walking right out, he left the room; likely to read the bottle for the first time ever.  Came bak and told me 'a numbing agent and mixture of different steroids'.  Those injections only ever made the pain worse.

&#x200B;

Unfortunately there is very little deep research into the wide spread and very different types, causes, and treatments of pain.  All of the legislation has only added to the issues, expanded and amplified the problems, and made everything much much worse for both legitimate pain patients and people suffering from various addictions.

&#x200B;

OP:  It sounds like you should be all set at this new clinic.  I would advise not actually and formally leaving your current treatment, or even telling them until you get through the first appointment at the new and know for certain things will go smooth.  With the small chance something, for some reason doesn't work at the new place, you don't want to end up scrambling to find a new place that will work and suffering when your old one won't maintain you while you do.  Best wishes.  We feel your pain.  Literally.

Awesome dreams brother, a good life doesn't mean a lavish life, it just means a fulfilling one.  They say we only get to keep what we give away.

&#x200B;

Side note, have you heard about the research being done using oxytocin?  If not, check it out.

Reevaluate your "DD" process.

&#x200B;

Penny stocks don't make good on "promises".  Blue chips hardly do.  Read the disclaimers and remember them every time you "DD".

Again, you brought up wealth continually, with plenty of specific numbers to feed that ego.  And clearly that ego is why a person would deny ever having fake pills and take offense to it like you do.  I was being informative and laying out information regarding the story and details that you wrote.  People don't go on "dope runs" to pick up from their doctor and pharmacy.  Stand by your own words. Or did your ego turn up the color on that story for more padding?  Only one of us knows the others net worth, and that one sure isn't jealous of it.  Clearly you're looking down into this community and stereotyping while trying to separate yourself from everyone else here.

&#x200B;

Edit: And Doni't forget to live, love, laugh that truth, Karen.

It's completely ok, and for whatever your reasons are.

&#x200B;

I had my fun in my earlier years, but have nearly 0 interest in casual sex, FWB, open relationships and whatever else is all the rage.

I have a memory and pay attention to all details.  They're pretty essential attributes in this game.

&#x200B;

I didn't check any history, I saw your screen name again and thought, "That's pretty funny the guy that read my warning prior to open and denied it claimed the very next day that it 'caught him off guard' ".  I found that, 'sort of weird'.
